{
  "_comment": [
    "The word-order regression net. Every sentence is an example from",
    "docs/word_order.md, tagged with the rule that names it and the side of",
    "that rule's examples it comes from (`outcome`: preferred or allowed).",
    "`features` pins the clause features the analysis must produce for that",
    "clause (index given by `clause`, default 0).",
    "",
    "`diagnostics` is the exact expected kind list. Every example here is",
    "correct Finnish, so it must stay clean: a word-order rule never reports",
    "it, and no other rule may fire on it either. `PREFER` is a generation",
    "preference, not an error.",
    "",
    "The `text` values must appear verbatim in tests/fixtures/word_order_rules.json;",
    "tests/word_order_allow.rs checks both direction and coverage."
  ],
